{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed","id":1043551,"title":"Should Frejya be Frigg in 2nd ed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T07:51:18-08:00","id":1043551,"title":"Should Frejya be Frigg in 2nd ed?","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So I noticed they conflated a lot of the Gods as being different mantles of the same being, so I am wondering if 2nd Ed is going to have Sekhmet be the same as Bast then it sounds like Frejya would work under this paradigm as the same Goddess as Frigg, as many researchers have argued was the case. That makes Odin the missing god Od, and that makes Frigg one of the Vanir, and things work much smoother explaining why Frejya gets to share half the Einherjar with Odin.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If this is the case though I would rather they change what they had in 1st Edition, where Frigg was actually secretly her hand maidens. I mean I would like at least some lesser </span></span></span><i>\u00e1synja/aesir</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:21:24-08:00","id":1043531,"title":"","content":"So I noticed they conflated a lot of the Gods as being different mantles of the same being, so I am wondering if 3rd Ed is going to have Sekhmet be the same as Bast then it sounds like Frejya would work under this paradigm as the same Goddess as Frigg, as many researchers have argued was the case. That makes Odin the missing god Od, and that makes Frigg one of the Vanir, and things work much smoother explaining why Frejya gets to share half the Einherjar with Odin.<br /> <br /> If this is the case though I would rather they change what they had in 1st Edition, where Frigg was actually secretly her hand maidens. I mean I would like at least some lesser <i>\u00e1synja/aesir</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:50:09-08:00","id":1043550,"title":"","content":"Damnit this was meant for the Scion Forum... wow...my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:56:31-08:00","id":1043555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed?p=1043550#post1043550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit this was meant for the Scion Forum... wow...my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, shouldn't it be 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:02:43-08:00","id":1043556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed?p=1043555#post1043555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, shouldn't it be 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I corrected that when I remade the thread. :P Lot of confusion! I just turned 30!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:21:17-08:00","id":1043562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed?p=1043556#post1043556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I corrected that when I remade the thread. :P Lot of confusion! I just turned 30!</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to turn 30 once, but could never get a handle on it *badoum psh*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:26:32-08:00","id":1043601,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hope not. The conflating of Bast and Sekhmet was met with pretty loud and definitive opposition, and I think we've made it clear to the devs that we want <i>more </i>deities in our Scion, not fewer. Besides that, the combination of Freya and Frigg is debated among scholars and in the myths, and the Aesir are short on Goddesses as it is, so keeping both of them works for flavour and &quot;accuracy&quot; (if you can use that term when we know so little of older faiths in the first place...).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:40:58-08:00","id":1043632,"title":"","content":"See, the interesting thing about that is that Frigg and Freyja are conflated by all the non-Norse Germanic tribes, but the Norse were very consistent on them being separate deities. <br /> <br /> So I'm strongly of the opinion that Frigg and Freyja should be kept separate because the pantheon featured in Scion is the Norse pantheon, which is the Germanic tribe that kept them separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:53:22-08:00","id":1043635,"title":"","content":"I was very much not a fan of loosing Sekhmet, but I wasn't aware the fans formed a consensus since we haven't even gotten the book out yet and many of the fans haven't even been made aware of the change from preview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed?p=1043632#post1043632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the interesting thing about that is that Frigg and Freyja are conflated by all the non-Norse Germanic tribes, but the Norse were very consistent on them being separate deities.<br /> <br /> So I'm strongly of the opinion that Frigg and Freyja should be kept separate because the pantheon featured in Scion is the Norse pantheon, which is the Germanic tribe that kept them separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>...not really we only have scraps of the Myths that existed, so saying they have been very consistently seperate individuals. Considering that most of Frejya's names are ambiguous feminine titles, and Frigg is also a mysterious figure only really talked about in her relations with Odin, like when they both adopted a different mortal child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:07:33-08:00","id":1043642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1043551-should-frejya-be-frigg-in-2nd-ed?p=1043635#post1043635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was very much not a fan of loosing Sekhmet, but I wasn't aware the fans formed a consensus since we haven't even gotten the book out yet and many of the fans haven't even been made aware of the change from preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was <i>extensive</i> fan feedback for the Nejter preview. Neall popped in to say &quot;Yeah, we're going to do some revisions on this, get in some more experts to consult. Hey, maybe we'll use this as a preview later on to show all of you backers how the Revising step in making a Pantheon&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:27:06-08:00","id":1043649,"title":"","content":"Cool. I have noted besides that, that they have revised a lot, like adding in Chaos because Trickster wasn't enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T23:24:10-08:00","id":1043870,"title":"","content":"I read at least one poem from the Eddas that had Freya and Frigg as very definitely separate figures in the same room...<br /> <br /> The Lokksenna for reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}